messages:
anya: Heads-up — i'm about to land a terraform change that splits ExternalSecrets by namespace and updates the vault path for the payments service. small rollout, but want a quick sanity check before i merge. PR: https://git.redwood/infra/terraform/pull/412 :eyes:

sam: quick skim — the shape looks fine. main Q: how are you handling the service account -> vault role mapping?

anya: plan is kubernetes auth role per namespace, e.g. payments-reader bound to payments SA. TF snippet i'm using:
```hcl
resource "external_secrets_secretstore" "vault_payments" {
  metadata {
    name = "vault-payments"
    namespace = "payments"
  }
  spec {
    provider {
      vault {
        server = "https://vault.redwood-internal"
        path = "secret/data/services/payments"
        auth {
          kubernetes {
            role = "payments-reader"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

leah: that makes sense. rotation question: will you rely on Vault rotate + ExternalSecrets resync, or do you plan a push refresh?

anya: Vault rotation will create a new version. ExternalSecrets is configured with `refreshInterval: 1m` for these services so they'll pick up changes quickly. we also expose a small webhook in infra to trigger an immediate refresh if we need to force it.

sam: ok good. two nitpicks: (1) ensure the SA is immutable (imagePullSecrets etc) so we don't accidentally swap in a different SA and lose access; (2) set `secretStoreRef.kind` explicitly in manifests so operator doesn't try cluster-wide store by mistake.

mike: also add a migration note — some namespaces previously used a shared `legacy-secrets` store. need a one-off ExternalSecret to copy current values into new namespace store before cutover. maybe a short script in the PR description.

anya: yep added migration step in PR + a `kubectl get externalsecret -n payments -o yaml > backup.yaml` line.

infra-bot: CI: terraform fmt/checks passed for changed files. plan output: will create 2 resources, update 1.

leah: one more: rotation policy should limit max versions to keep Vault storage sane. we usually set `max_versions = 10` for service secrets.

anya: good call, i'll add that and re-run plan. leaving TODO to add tests for SA binding (integration smoke).

sam: ping me on the PR once you update, i'll do the review tonight. :+1:

anya: thanks — updated, PTAL. tagging @sam @mike for final check.

mike: LGTM from infra side, small comment in PR about docs.

anya: merging after CI green + infra smoke. will post cutover timeline in #eng-oncall later today. :thumbsup:
